{"experiments":[  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Unprotected reefs exhibit higher year-to-year species turnover (beta diversity) than protected reefs, indicating less community stability under exploitation.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Quantify and compare temporal beta diversity (compositional turnover) between consecutive years for reefs under different protection statuses.",  
      "steps":"1. From reef.csv, create presence/absence matrices of species for each reef×year at the reef scale (aggregate across transects).\n2. For each reef, compute pairwise Jaccard dissimilarity between years t and t+1.\n3. Compile a dataset with one dissimilarity value per reef×(year interval) and attach protection_status.\n4. Fit a mixed-effects model: dissimilarity ~ protection_status + (1|id_reef), or test protection_status effects via ANOVA.\n5. If significant, perform post-hoc pairwise comparisons among protection statuses.\n6. Plot mean dissimilarity by protection_status with error bars.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Table of average year-to-year Jaccard dissimilarity by protection_status with statistical test results.\n2. Mixed-effects model summary or ANOVA table.\n3. Bar plot of temporal turnover by protection_status (mean ± SE).\n4. Interpretation of whether unprotected reefs turnover faster."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Unprotected reefs have greater within-reef spatial heterogeneity in total fish biomass across transects than protected reefs, reflecting patchy fishing impacts.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Assess whether protection status influences the coefficient of variation (CV) of biomass among transects within each reef-year.",  
      "steps":"1. Using reef.csv, compute total biomass per transect (sum biomass within each id_reef, year, stratum, transect).\n2. For each reef-year, calculate the mean and standard deviation of transect biomass, then CV = SD/mean.\n3. Assemble a dataset of CV values with corresponding protection_status, reef, and year.\n4. Fit a linear mixed model: CV ~ protection_status + (1|id_reef).\n5. Test for significant differences among protection_status levels.\n6. Visualize CV distributions by protection_status.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Summary statistics of CV by protection_status.\n2. Mixed-effects model output testing CV ~ protection_status.\n3. Violin or box plot of CV across protection statuses.\n4. Narrative interpretation of spatial heterogeneity patterns."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Variance in individual fish body length per reef-year has increased over time more sharply at unprotected reefs, indicating a widening size spectrum under exploitation.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test whether the temporal trend in length variance differs by protection_status.",  
      "steps":"1. From reef.csv, for each id_reef×year, gather all individual lengths (size) across all transects.\n2. Compute the variance of size per reef-year.\n3. Create a dataset of size_variance, year, id_reef, and protection_status.\n4. Fit a linear mixed model: size_variance ~ year * protection_status + (1|id_reef).\n5. Examine the interaction term to see if unprotected reefs show a steeper increase.\n6. Plot size_variance vs. year stratified by protection_status with regression lines.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Mixed-effects model summary for size_variance.\n2. Table of estimated year slopes by protection_status.\n3. Line plot of variance over time by protection_status.\n4. Interpretation of how length‐variance trends differ with protection."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Shallow depth strata host a higher proportion of small‐bodied fish (<10 cm) than deeper strata, and this depth‐size pattern is more pronounced at unprotected reefs.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Evaluate how the proportion of small fish varies with depth stratum and whether protection modifies this relationship.",  
      "steps":"1. From reef.csv, classify each record as small if size<10 cm.\n2. For each id_reef×year×stratum, sum small_count and total_count and compute prop_small.\n3. Label each record with depth stratum (e.g. shallow vs deep) and protection_status.\n4. Fit a binomial GLMM: small_count | total_count ~ stratum * protection_status + (1|id_reef).\n5. Test for significant stratum×protection interactions.\n6. Plot predicted prop_small vs. stratum for each protection_status with 95% CIs.",  
      "deliverables":"1. GLMM summary table with fixed‐effect coefficients and interactions.\n2. Post‐hoc contrasts of stratum effects within each protection_status.\n3. Dot‐and‐whisker plot of prop_small by stratum and protection_status.\n4. Interpretation of depth effects on size structure."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Mean individual biomass (biomass per fish) has declined over time at unprotected reefs relative to protected reefs, evidencing fishing down the size spectrum.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Compare temporal trends in average individual fish biomass across protection statuses.",  
      "steps":"1. From reef.csv, for each id_reef×year, compute total_biomass and total_count, then avg_biomass = total_biomass/total_count.\n2. Build a dataset with avg_biomass, year, protection_status, and id_reef.\n3. Fit a linear mixed model: avg_biomass ~ year * protection_status + (1|id_reef).\n4. Examine interaction to see if unprotected reefs show a sharper decline.\n5. Plot avg_biomass vs. year by protection_status with model fits.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Mixed model summary for avg_biomass.\n2. Table of year‐by‐status slopes and confidence intervals.\n3. Time‐series plot of avg_biomass by protection_status.\n4. Discussion of fishing effects on individual biomass."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"The exponent (slope) of the size‐abundance relationship (size spectrum) has become steeper over time at unprotected reefs compared to protected reefs.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Estimate size‐spectrum slopes per reef-year and test for temporal changes by protection_status.",  
      "steps":"1. Bin individual sizes into logarithmically spaced bins (e.g. midpoints at 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 cm).\n2. For each id_reef×year, count individuals per size bin and compute log10(count) vs log10(size_mid).\n3. Fit a linear regression per reef-year: log10(count) ~ log10(size_mid) and extract slope.\n4. Compile slopes into a dataset with year, id_reef, protection_status.\n5. Fit linear mixed model: slope ~ year * protection_status + (1|id_reef).\n6. Test if unprotected reefs show a significant temporal steepening.\n7. Visualize size‐spectrum slopes over time by protection_status.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Table of size‐spectrum slopes per reef-year.\n2. Mixed‐effects model results for slope ~ year * protection_status.\n3. Line plot of spectral slopes over time by protection_status.\n4. Interpretation of changes in community size structure."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"The proportion of core species (those present in ≥50% of transects) within a reef-year has decreased over time more at unprotected reefs than at protected reefs.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Assess whether fishing reduces the stability of species occurrence by comparing core‐species proportions over time.",  
      "steps":"1. From reef.csv, identify transect IDs per reef-year (4 replicates per stratum).\n2. For each reef-year, tabulate species presence across transects and compute core_species = number of species present in ≥50% of transects.\n3. Compute total_species = number of species detected.\n4. Compute prop_core = core_species/total_species.\n5. Build dataset with prop_core, year, id_reef, protection_status.\n6. Fit mixed model: prop_core ~ year * protection_status + (1|id_reef).\n7. Test interactions and plot prop_core over time by protection_status.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Mixed model summary for prop_core.\n2. Yearly estimates of core‐species proportions by protection_status.\n3. Plot of prop_core vs. year by protection_status.\n4. Interpretation of species occurrence stability."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Within-reef compositional dissimilarity among depth strata (spatial beta diversity) decreases over time at protected reefs, indicating management-driven community homogenization.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Measure spatial beta diversity among strata within each reef-year and test temporal trends by protection.",  
      "steps":"1. For each reef-year, build species abundance matrices for each depth stratum.\n2. Compute pairwise Bray-Curtis dissimilarity among strata and average them to get a single spatial beta diversity metric per reef-year.\n3. Compile a dataset of spatial_beta, year, id_reef, protection_status.\n4. Fit linear mixed model: spatial_beta ~ year * protection_status + (1|id_reef).\n5. Test whether protected reefs show declining beta diversity (homogenization) over time compared to unprotected.\n6. Plot spatial_beta vs. year for each protection_status.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Table of spatial beta diversity per reef-year.\n2. Mixed model results for spatial_beta trends.\n3. Time series plot of spatial_beta by protection_status.\n4. Interpretation of depth-stratum homogenization patterns."  
    }  
  }  
]}
